@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@
+# Independent OOD generator 0.1
+
+The entry point is `agent_loop_lab.synth_ood.FAMILIES`. Every entry accepts
+`(rng: random.Random, session_id: str, cfg: OracleConfig)` and returns
+`(list[CanonicalEvent], OracleRecord)`. No standard generator implementation,
+datasets, classifiers, weights, network services, or material outside this
+commission directory was consulted.
+
+## World and causal model
+
+`engine.py` implements an in-memory repository with actual text contents. A
+small contract language interprets `enabled=1` as a satisfied shard predicate;
+`enabled=0` is a fault. Each shard also has a `mode` convention. Comments are
+behaviourally inert. Test counts are computed from these predicates, and
+progress is the fraction of satisfied contracts. This is a simulated language
+interpreter, not execution of Elixir, Zig, Lua, or Clojure. Those extensions,
+paths and suite names supply varied tool vocabulary.
+
+Each read of an unexplored contract reveals two material facts: its predicate
+and fixture. The engine maintains a knowledge set, content read history,
+behavioural validation history, control history, previous workspace digests,
+one active episode, and independent mirror/index readiness counters. Different
+request bodies distinguish service retries; backoff metadata does not.
+External success reveals lease knowledge but does not repair repository faults.
+
+Effects come from these state transitions, never from fingerprints or encoded
+features. The initial failure opens no episode. An exact consecutive retry
+opens one; retries/polls consume the supplied config's budgets. Success closes
+the episode and takes precedence over new knowledge. A relevant behavioural
+change closes an abandoned episode immediately; two unrelated operations also
+close it. Progress belongs to the write, never to its subsequent validation.
+Comment churn is redundant despite changing text digests. A return to a prior
+content state records an undo; the shared labeller recomputes reversions for
+each window. Progress, facts and undo flags remain recorded even when a higher
+precedence effect applies.
+
+Canonical digests and fingerprints use only the shared fingerprint module.
+Public events contain operation metadata and observations, with no scenario
+tags or hidden effects. Session identifiers are caller supplied: callers should
+use opaque identifiers when assembling evaluation sets. The sealed record uses
+`generator_version="ood-0.1"`, `scenario_family="ood:<name>"`, and exactly the
+shared `latent_trace` and `label_session` functions. Since the API supplies an
+RNG rather than its original seed, `OracleRecord.seed` is a stream nonce drawn
+from that RNG. Replay requires the caller's original seed or saved RNG state;
+the nonce is not advertised as a replay seed.
+
+## Families
+
+Intended mixes below are minimum scored-label coverage in each session under
+the frozen v0.2 parameters. Ambiguous transition windows are retained. The
+instrumentation family additionally has unscored instrumentation labels.
+
+| Family | Intended scored labels | Mechanics and difference from §7.1 |
+|---|---|---|
+| `shard_migration` | PRODUCTIVE | Reconcile independently broken shard contracts in random order. Each write repairs a predicate and each replica test derives new counts from text. Reimagines incremental repair and improving repeated validation (§7.1.1, 9) as distributed contract migration. |
+| `fixture_archaeology` | PRODUCTIVE | Investigate separate shard predicates and fixture identities, interspersed with distinct planning operations, before making edits. Reimagines exploration (§7.1.2) as material fixture discovery rather than repeated diagnostics. |
+| `lease_reconnect` | RECOVERY, PRODUCTIVE | Several distinct mirror hosts reset lease POST requests two or three times before accepting them; repair surrounds the external episodes. Reimagines transient failures and bounded retries (§7.1.3, 4) through multi-host lease acquisition. |
+| `index_watermark` | RECOVERY, PRODUCTIVE | Distinct replicated indexes return neutral not-ready results, then a lease becomes visible. Backoff changes on every poll but remains outside intent identity. Reimagines legitimate repeated polling (§7.1.10) as sequential quorum-watermark waits. |
+| `pinned_validation` | RECOVERY, STALLED | Select a replica check, then repeatedly invoke the same deterministic failing suite without changing behaviour. The prelude lets early in-policy retries fall inside full windows. Reimagines repeated failed tests (§7.1.5) as a pinned replica assertion that survives far beyond the retry budget. |
+| `annotation_spiral` | STALLED | Append fresh explanatory comments with changing ticket numbers, validating between writes. Every digest is fresh but behaviour and pass counts are fixed. Reimagines ineffective edits and expensive repetition (§7.1.6, 11) as documentation-only repair attempts. |
+| `serializer_duel` | OSCILLATING | Two emitters alternately restore left/right wire conventions in one contract. Neither satisfies any fault predicate. Reimagines workspace/tool oscillation (§7.1.7, 8) as opposing serializers rather than alternative fixes. |
+| `merge_ping_pong` | OSCILLATING | Alternate upstream/local ownership resolutions in a merge configuration, with reconciliation plans between writes. **Additional family absent from the §7.1 list:** merge ownership negotiation rather than a repair task. The simulated conflicting choices are concrete file contents; no real git merge is run. |
+| `lockfile_churn` | OSCILLATING | Installer and resolver alternately pin dependency versions 1 and 2, inspecting the result after each write. **Additional family absent from the §7.1 list:** dependency pin negotiation. Dependency changes do not satisfy shard predicates; no package manager is invoked. |
+| `telemetry_gaps` | PRODUCTIVE | Continue contract repair while independently losing one failure fingerprint, one workspace observation, and one token observation. Reimagines under-instrumentation (§7.1.12) as isolated transport gaps with fully intact latent state and recovery of gate coverage. |
+
+## Distribution choices and instrumentation
+
+The repository has 12–18 contracts, with four language/suite vocabularies,
+varying error classes and generated mirror/resource identities. Family session
+lengths range from 24 to 89 events, with longer plateau and oscillation tails
+than the standard spec's 12–60-event envelope. Ordering, counts, costs,
+timestamps, vocabulary, and service readiness all use the passed RNG. There
+are no global RNG calls, wall-clock reads or I/O during generation.
+
+Costs are zero with probability 0.13; otherwise they are lognormal with
+parameters `(7.5, 1.65)`, capped at 400,000 tokens and divided randomly between
+input/output. This distribution is independent of labels and can exceed the
+encoder's saturation threshold. High spend is not a stall rule.
+
+Missing validation baselines can contaminate later windows. To satisfy the
+commission's exact window-local rejection requirement, telemetry gaps drop
+tokens, workspace digests and failure fingerprints, while retaining suite/count
+observations and complete history. Thus a window fails the gate exactly while
+it contains a dropped event, without causing later baseline rejection.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run from this directory:
+
+```sh
+PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests_ood -q
+```
+
+The tests cover all ten families over 24 seeds, byte-identical event and sealed
+record serialization, schema round trips, sequence validation, latent
+validation, label recomputation, effect/dropped-index consistency, intended
+label coverage per session, and every full window's gate/encoder path.
+Focused causal checks exercise content-derived progress and test results,
+knowledge, redundant edits, retry/poll limits, resolution precedence,
+abandonment, reversions and all three intentional missing-observation reasons.
+Labels are never selected by examining encoded feature values.
